# Meteofy

React 18, Vite 5, JavaScript (JSX). No TypeScript, Next.js, or Tailwind.

- `src/main.jsx` mounts the Redux store and `App`.
- `src/pages` are route screens. Paths live in `src/utils/constants/routes.js` and are registered in `src/routes`.
- `src/components` holds UI. A folder contains `Name.jsx` and, when styled, `Name.styles.jsx`.
- `src/services/api` fetches weather and geocoding. Endpoint details live in `src/utils/constants/api`.
- `src/state` is Redux Toolkit: `cityData` for the selected city, `themeData` for dark mode.
- `src/hooks` and `src/utils` hold shared logic, formatters, chart config, and city lists.
- `src/utils/styles` holds the styled-components theme and global styles.
- `public/` holds static assets such as weather icons.

Routing is React Router 6. Styles are styled-components with the existing light and dark theme. Maps are Leaflet (Europe), SVG (Poland), and React Three Fiber (world). Charts use Chart.js. The city popup is SweetAlert2 in `src/components/ui/modals/WeatherModal`. HTTP uses axios.

Scripts: `npm run dev`, `npm run build`, `npm run preview`, `npm run lint` (zero warnings), `npm run format`.
